Z||000001||KRMFiero||07-28-2001||05:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>is the normal 3 speed automatic transmission in any way computer controlled?<P>As far as i know it is not, just it has wires for the startign positions (Park, Nutral and then the reverse light)<P>what does the linkage on the throttlebody do for it?  shift harder, shift points...etc..<P>Isnt it the kick down cable? im not sure...<P>would it overheat on a 3.2 stroker staying in 1st gear at 3000 rpms for 10 minutes?<P>why would you stay at 3000 rpm for 10 minutes in first? your engine might over heat, i dont think the tranny would but if you plan to do that i would add another tranny cooler and a engine oil cooler <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
